- op: discuss  # aef2
  at: '2026-05-30T09:06:43Z'  # aef2
  by: agent  # aef2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # aef2
  clock: 3  # aef2
  nonce: aef2  # aef2
  message: "Cross-ref backfill (2026-05-30, deeper-issue investigation): Same writer-side root cause as INV-nuzal (edge.provenance/quality empty 100%) and INV-pitab (per-pass provenance field set does not carry consumer-needed data) — three faces of \"schema reserves slot for evidence-derived metadata, emitters write constants or nothing.\" ir.py:563 sets confidence: float = 0.85 as the canonical default, signaling the convention is a single number, and no confidence_source field exists in IR to distinguish calibrated from fallback. py.py:1988-3242 confirms 5+ hardcoded values across (edge-type, evidence-type) tuples. Two-state derivation pattern emerging in some linkers (cgo.py:189, jni.py:266, kafka_streams_dispatch.py:373: confidence = 0.5 if is_fallback else 0.X) is a partial fix shape worth generalizing. Candidate umbrella: \"evidence-derived metadata never gets emitted\" covering this + INV-nuzal + INV-pitab. Fix candidate: introduce confidence_source: Literal[\"evidence_derived\", \"hardcoded_fallback\"] with # axis: bounded-enum so consumers can filter."  # aef2
- op: discuss  # 11d8
  at: '2026-06-02T03:21:39Z'  # 11d8
  by: agent  # 11d8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 11d8
  clock: 4  # 11d8
  nonce: 11d8  # 11d8
  message: "Pass-21 confirmation observations (F4 + F5) — see ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06012026_2310_pass21.md.\n\n**F4: `evidence_type=naming_convention` uses confidence=1.0 across all 18,291 such edges.** Naming-convention is a heuristic inference (e.g., `test_foo → tests foo`); confidence=1.0 means \"we are maximally confident the edge is real,\" which is incompatible with heuristic evidence. This is a particularly egregious instance of the hardcoded-per-emitter pattern this invariant tracks: not only is the value hardcoded, the value chosen (1.0) is the LEAST defensible for the evidence_type involved.\n\n**F5: Same evidence_type produces multiple distinct confidence values across edges.** Re-measured on pass-21 substrate (post-INV-sugat-closure):\n\n| evidence_type | edges | distinct confidence values |\n|---|---|---|\n| ast_call_direct | 35,540 | 5 (0.5 / 0.7 / 0.85 / 0.9 / 0.95) |\n| ast_call | 21,376 | 4 (0.4 / 0.5 / 0.8 / 0.95) |\n| ast_decorator | 402 | 2 (0.5 / 0.95) |\n\nThis is the same pattern this invariant already tracks — same evidence type ≠ same confidence — but at a finer grain than the original Phase-1 (edge-type) bucket. Suggests two equally valid framings:\n- evidence_type is too coarse — sub-divide into resolved/fallback variants (e.g., `ast_call_direct_resolved` vs `ast_call_direct_recovery`)\n- confidence is decoupled from evidence_type entirely — confidence reflects emitter origin or call-target ambiguity, not evidence type\n\nEither framing means the validator's cross_field class could add an invariant: \"every evidence_type maps to a documented confidence range, not a value, and every emitter using that evidence_type stays within the range.\""  # 11d8
